   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Greening the Central Bank of Eswatini &amp; Capacity Building-UNDP-SWZ-01001487</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Central Banks play critical roles in promoting greening of the economy and addressing the climate change risks. Central banks can provide guidance and support to financial institutions on how to green their operations and products. This guidance can include information on climate change risks, green finance products, and best practices for greening financial services. Specific areas in which a central bank can provide this guidance is through taking the lead in adopting green policies and practices such as in investing in green technologies, reducing their carbon footprint, and supporting green initiatives in the community. Central banks can also foster collaboration between financial institutions and other stakeholders such as governments, businesses, and non-governmental organizations and help to develop and implement green finance solutions that address climate change risks. Further, Central banks can promote research and development to develop new green finance products and services, and to improve the un</narrative>
  </description>
